# The published page is compared byte for byte by the CI drift guard and by the test beside
# it. The build writes LF explicitly so a rebuild matches on any OS; without this line a
# Windows checkout converts the committed copy to CRLF and every local rebuild then reports
# a stale page for a reason no commit caused.
docs/index.html text eol=lf

# The demo log is scanned by the page build and its timestamps are compared against the
# committed page; a checkout that rewrote its line endings would not change the findings,
# but keeping it stable removes one more source of a spurious diff.
sample/*.log text eol=lf
